<BaseLayout title="Umrah Cost Calculator — Quote-Based Budget Planner" description="Build an Umrah budget from current package and supplier quotes, separating per-traveller costs from shared accommodation and transport."><article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10"><h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4">Umrah Cost Calculator</h1><p class="mb-8">Build an Umrah budget from current package and supplier quotes, separating per-traveller costs from shared accommodation and transport.</p><Calculator client:load /><section class="prose max-w-none mt-10"><h2>Use your actual quotes</h2><p>Enter the quoted airfare, visa/services and insurance per person. Accommodation and transfer rows are totals for the group, so they are added once. Enter meals and contingency per person. All rows must use the selected currency.</p><h2>Avoid double-counting a package</h2><p>If a package already includes hotels, transfers or insurance, put its relevant total in one row and zero in included rows. Check room occupancy, dates, meals, cancellation conditions and which services are actually confirmed. A budget result does not establish visa or permit approval.</p><h2>Understand the result</h2><p>Per-person rows are multiplied by the traveller count; shared rows are added once. The total is divided by the number of travellers for the average per-person budget. Changing currency clears amounts because this planner does not convert prices.</p><p>For example, a shared transfer of 10,000 in the selected currency is 10,000 for the group, not 10,000 for every person. Check whether your supplier quotes per room, per traveller or for the whole group before entering a number.</p><h2>Keep a planning record</h2><p>Save the supplier name, quote date, validity, inclusions and cancellation terms with your budget. Enter zero where a cost does not apply. No unverified default fares, visa prices or insurance premiums are supplied here.</p><p>Use our <a href="/tools/visa-fee-calculator/">visa fee service</a> and <a href="/guides/">travel guides</a> for the next checks. Calculations remain in your browser.</p></section></article></BaseLayout>
